  "title": "Coast Guard medevacs citizen of India from tanker off Oahu",
  "description": "An MH-65 Dolphin helicopter crew from Coast Guard Air Station Barbers Point safely hoists a 54-year-old citizen of India from the 1,050-foot Bahamian-flagged oil tanker Andromeda Voyager at first light Aug. 10, 2016, 14 miles south of Oahu. The man was suffering from symptoms of a hart attack and was transferred him to Queen’s Medical Center in Honolulu in stable condition. (U.S. Coast Guard video by Coast Guard Air Station Barbers Point CG 6608/Released)",
